                "High-Risk and Subjective Exclusions: Under both ISA 610 and PCAOB AS 2605, the external auditor is strictly prohibited from relying on internal audit for areas involving high degrees of judgment, significant risk of material misstatement, or complex management estimates (such as goodwill impairment valuations or significant fraud investigations under ISA 240). The external auditor must make all significant professional judgments and bears sole, indivisible responsibility for the audit opinion.",
